================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

Reelsi does not bundle any third-party code or model weights. Everything listed
below is installed by the user via pip, downloaded at runtime, or invoked as a
separate program. Licenses are those declared by each upstream project; verify
them against upstream before redistributing a build.

--- Runtime dependencies (pip) ---

PyTorch, torchaudio, torchvision      BSD-3-Clause    https://pytorch.org
Flask                                 BSD-3-Clause    https://flask.palletsprojects.com
NumPy, SciPy                          BSD-3-Clause    https://numpy.org, https://scipy.org
soundfile                             BSD-3-Clause    https://github.com/bastibe/python-soundfile
librosa                               ISC             https://librosa.org
questionary                           MIT             https://github.com/tmbo/questionary
faster-whisper (CTranslate2)          MIT             https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
transformers, accelerate              Apache-2.0      https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
huggingface-hub                       Apache-2.0      https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface_hub
qwen-omni-utils                       Apache-2.0      https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5-Omni
Pillow                                MIT-CMU (HPND)  https://python-pillow.org
fontTools                             MIT             https://github.com/fonttools/fonttools
rembg                                 MIT             https://github.com/danielgatis/rembg
anthropic (Python SDK)                MIT             https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python
silero-vad                            MIT             https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
scikit-learn                          BSD-3-Clause    https://scikit-learn.org
pytest                                MIT             https://pytest.org

--- Model weights (downloaded on demand, never bundled) ---

Whisper large-v3 (OpenAI)             MIT
Qwen2.5-Omni (Alibaba)                Apache-2.0      https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5-Omni
GigaAM (Sber / salute-developers)     see upstream    https://github.com/salute-developers/GigaAM
CED-tiny (mispeech/ced-tiny)          Apache-2.0      https://huggingface.co/mispeech/ced-tiny
Robust Video Matting (PeterL1n)       GPL-3.0         https://github.com/PeterL1n/RobustVideoMatting

Robust Video Matting is loaded through torch.hub, which fetches both weights and
upstream code at runtime. GPL-3.0 is compatible with AGPL-3.0, so combining them
is permitted; the resulting combined work is governed by the AGPL. If the
roto feature is never used, nothing from RVM is downloaded or loaded.

--- External programs (invoked as subprocesses, not linked) ---

ffmpeg          LGPL-2.1+ or GPL-2+ depending on build   https://ffmpeg.org
                Must be present in PATH; Reelsi does not ship it.
yt-dlp          Unlicense                                https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
                Called as `python -m yt_dlp` for background music. Downloading
                third-party content may violate a platform's terms of service and
                copyright law; responsibility rests with the user.
rclone          MIT                                      https://rclone.org
                Must be installed separately (not pip); used to download material
                from a Google Drive link. Credentials live in the user's own
                rclone config (`REELSI_RCLONE_CONF`), never in Reelsi files.

--- Trademarks and proprietary assets ---

Adobe, After Effects, and Premiere Pro are trademarks of Adobe Inc. Reelsi is
neither affiliated with nor endorsed by Adobe. Interoperability is achieved
solely through published formats: FCP7 XML and ExtendScript.

SF Pro is a proprietary Apple typeface. It is NOT distributed with Reelsi. The
subtitle templates in refblobs.json reference the PostScript font name
